    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0477" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1028.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Blanchard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-24T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order that there may be no misconstruction of the Department’s November 21, 7
                    p.m., the Government of the United States will formally recognize Theodore as
                    President of Haiti as soon as Haitian Commission in Washington has signed
                    satisfactory protocols covering all matters mentioned in Department’s November
                    12, 2 p.m. and November 13, 3 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d550-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d550-f1" n="6" xml:id="d550-f1-content">
                <p>There is no such instruction on file. The telegram of Nov. 16, 11 a.m., in reply
                    to the Minister’s Nov. 13, 3 p.m., is doubtless the one meant.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
